card.statement:
The basis of the module in the previous theorem is

\begin{gather*}
{\mathcal B}(T(L)) = \big\{T(L+z):z\in\mathbb{Z}^{\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}~\text{and}~z_{n1}=\cdots=z_{nn}=0\big\}.
\end{gather*}

By a slight abuse of notation we will identify elements in $\mathbb{Z}^{\frac{n(n-1)}{2}}$ with elements $z\in\mathbb{Z}^{\frac{n(n+1)}{2}}$ such that $z_{n1}=\cdots=z_{nn}=0$. This will allow us to write $T(L+z)$ for $z\in\mathbb{Z}^{\frac{n(n-1)}{2}}$.
